<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>CryptStorage client download</title>
<style>
  :root { color-scheme: dark; --bg:#0a0e14; --fg:#d7dde5; --muted:#8a96a6; --accent:#00e5a0; --line:#1e2733; }
  body { margin:0; background:var(--bg); color:var(--fg); font:15px/1.55 system-ui, sans-serif; }
  main { max-width:820px; margin:0 auto; padding:24px 16px 64px; }
  h1 { font-size:1.5rem; margin:.2em 0 .6em; }
  h2 { font-size:1.1rem; margin:1.8em 0 .5em; }
  a { color:var(--accent); }
  code, pre { font-family:ui-monospace, monospace; font-size:.88em; }
  pre { background:#111821; border:1px solid var(--line); padding:10px 12px; overflow-x:auto; }
  table { width:100%; border-collapse:collapse; }
  td, th { text-align:left; padding:8px 6px; border-bottom:1px solid var(--line); vertical-align:top; }
  .sum { word-break:break-all; color:var(--muted); font-size:.8em; }
  .note { border:1px solid #ffb020; background:rgba(255,176,32,.07); padding:10px 12px; }
  .muted { color:var(--muted); }
</style>
</head>
{% set names = download_files | map('basename') | list %}
{% set exe = names | select('search', '(?i)setup.*\\.exe$') | first | default('') %}
{% set deb = names | select('search', '\\.deb$') | first | default('') %}
<body>
<main>
<h1>CryptStorage client</h1>
<p>The client encrypts your files on your own computer before they reach this server
({{ domain }}). Connecting needs your password and your USB key stick.</p>
<p class="note">Pre-release software, not independently audited. The programs are not code-signed, so
Windows SmartScreen may warn about them. Check the SHA-256 sum before you run anything.</p>
<p>The official releases, with a signed <code>SHA256SUMS</code>, are on
<a href="https://github.com/valveo/cryptstorage/releases">GitHub</a>; how to check the signature:
<a href="https://github.com/valveo/cryptstorage/blob/main/docs/verify-release.md">docs/verify-release.md</a>.
The files below should have the same SHA-256 sums as the release of the same version.</p>

<h2>Files</h2>
<table>
  <tr><th>File</th><th>Size</th></tr>
{% for s in download_stats.results %}
  <tr>
    <td><a href="{{ s.item | basename | urlencode }}">{{ s.item | basename }}</a>
        <div class="sum">SHA-256 {{ s.stat.checksum }}</div></td>
    <td>{{ (s.stat.size / 1048576) | round(1) }} MB</td>
  </tr>
{% endfor %}
</table>
<p><a href="SHA256SUMS">SHA256SUMS</a> (all of the above in one file)</p>

<h2>Windows 10 or newer</h2>
<p>Run the <code>Setup</code> file. It also installs the components the client needs (WinFsp, SSHFS-Win,
Dokan) and the CryptStorage tray icon. Then choose <b>Set up CryptStorage...</b> from the tray menu
(or run <code>cryptclient setup</code> in a command prompt); it walks you through the account, the USB stick
and the recovery code. Afterwards the tray icon connects when you insert the stick.</p>
{% if exe %}<p>Check the file first; the sum must match the one above:</p>
<pre>(Get-FileHash .\{{ exe }}).Hash.ToLower()</pre>{% endif %}

<h2>Linux (Ubuntu, Debian)</h2>
<pre>sha256sum -c --ignore-missing SHA256SUMS
sudo apt install ./{{ deb or 'cryptclient_VERSION_amd64.deb' }}
cryptclient setup</pre>

<h2>Server</h2>
<p>Server address for the client: <code>https://{{ domain }}/api</code> (typing just <code>{{ domain }}</code> works too)</p>
{% if server_pin is defined and server_pin.stdout | default('') %}
<p>The client saves the server's TLS key pin on the stick when you set it up. It should be
<code class="sum">sha256/{{ server_pin.stdout }}</code></p>
{% endif %}
<p class="muted">Source code: <a href="{{ source_url | default('https://github.com/valveo/cryptstorage') }}">{{ source_url | default('https://github.com/valveo/cryptstorage') }}</a></p>
</main>
</body>
</html>
